Comment: MeshForge is a final-year student project. The team has not chosen a
 license for its own code yet; until it does, all rights are reserved by its
 authors. The package bundles third-party software under its own licenses:
 a python-build-standalone build of CPython (Python Software Foundation
 License; its bundled libraries' notices are under
 /opt/meshforge/controller/<version>/python/), Python packages whose license
 texts ship inside their *.dist-info folders under
 /opt/meshforge/controller/<version>/python/lib/python3.12/site-packages/, and
 a trimmed relocatable build of PostgreSQL 16 (theseus-rs/postgresql-binaries;
 PostgreSQL License, a liberal BSD/MIT-style license) under
 /opt/meshforge/controller/<version>/pgsql/ - its COPYRIGHT and LICENSE files
 and the notices of the libraries it bundles (OpenSSL 3: Apache-2.0; ICU:
 Unicode-3.0; zlib, zstd, lz4, libxml2: their own permissive licenses) are kept
 there (pgsql/COPYRIGHT, pgsql/LICENSE, pgsql/dependency-notices/). GNU
 readline (GPL-3, linked only by psql) is not shipped: psql is trimmed out.

